course: dictionary
lesson: 1182
title: Brown: a colour, a cooking word, and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word brown does three jobs. As an adjective it describes a thing: «Her eyes are brown.» As a noun it names the colour: «Brown is the colour of chocolate.» As a verb it means to cook something until its outside turns brown: «Brown the onions for five minutes.»
explain: To find the job, look at the words around brown. If it describes something, it comes before a noun like bread or paper, or after is or are. If someone is cooking, look for a verb like brown, browned or browning. Then ask: are we talking about a colour, or about cooking?
explain: Brown can also change form to show more or most: «The leaves are browner than yesterday.» Browner compares two things, and brownest is for three or more, just like bigger and biggest. Brown in the word «brown paper» is still a colour, even when it is part of a bigger phrase.
fact: Brown is the colour of chocolate, wood and soil.
fact: Brown can be an adjective, a noun or a verb.
fact: To brown food is to cook it until its outside turns brown, like toast or onions.
fact: Brown's comparison forms are browner and brownest.
fact: «The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog» is a pangram, a sentence that uses every letter of the alphabet at least once.
exercise: Mum says, «Brown the onions for five minutes.» What does brown mean in this sentence? | To paint them brown | To cut them into thin rings | *To cook until the outside turns brown | To wash them in cold water
exercise: «Her eyes are brown, and mine are browner.» What kind of word is browner? | *An adjective that compares two things | A verb meaning to cook | A noun that names a colour | A name for a person
exercise: «The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog» is famous because it is what? | *A pangram, using every letter of the alphabet | A poem about a fox and a dog | A recipe for brown toast
test: «We bought brown paper to wrap the parcel.» What is brown doing in this sentence? | Cooking the paper in a pan | Naming a bird | *Describing the paper and telling its colour | Making the paper go soft
test: «Sam browned the chicken in a hot pan.» Which word is the verb? | pan | *browned | chicken | hot
exam: «Leaf insects have flat bodies with brown spots like bite marks.» What does brown describe here? | *The spots, as a colour | The leaves, when they are cooked | The bite marks, as a verb | The insects, as they eat
